      "headline": "Engineering Director, Global Distribution Automation",
      "about": "I am a supply chain engineer with a record of successfully designing and deploying innovative automated solutions to multiple distribution networks, to deliver a competitive advantage in a highly competitive and evolving supply chain landscape.\n\nI am passionate about innovative technology and building highly usable, scalable, and intelligent enterprise solutions to solve business problems related to supply chains, distribution, and fulfillment.\n\nAs a proud graduate of the Clemson University with a degree in Industrial Engineering, I have leveraged my coursework and continued to build skills in Financial Modeling, Network Design, Strategic Planning, ASRS & Product Design, People Management, Talent Development, and Influence & Communication.\n\nI am currently Engineering Program Director, Global Distribution Automation, at Medtronic where I am responsible for driving network design and financial modeling to deliver a transformed supply chain.\n\nI live with my family in Durham, NC and I am always happy to learn more about innovative products or solutions that will continue making disruptions in the supply chain market.",
